A||||4||Simple Fiero||TBI question||||5||
Z||000000||Simple Fiero||09-05-2001||06:48 PM||||Okay here is the thing, I was trying to find something on my throttle body by looking in my haynes manual, and guess what my throttle body doesn't look anything like the one in the book, but I am a little smart and figured out what was what, (with help of haynes). Then I thought what the hell i will look at my dad's truck.(92 s-10 4cyl) And guess what, mine is the same as his, I friggin dentical! Now I am totally confused. So when I order parts for my throttle body do I order S-10 sensors and stuff, now my car is an 88. Is it possible that I have the wrong one? Are all the 88's this way. <BR>It says GM TBI right on it. Another question I have is can I take the air cleaner and manifold from a 92 S-10 and put it on my car or is that going to mess everything up.<BR>Thanks Craig<P>88 SC 4cyl 5speed||||reg||5
Z||000001||DRH||09-05-2001||07:20 PM||||87 and 88 have a different throttle body than 84-86. The Haynes manual MAY show it in the update section in the back.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroPerformance||09-05-2001||07:25 PM||||I have an 85 GT. What is my throttle body supposed to say on it?<P>-Charlie||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||09-05-2001||07:27 PM||||Haynes Fiero book has NO coverage of that motor beyond the balance unit in 88 motors.<P>The TBI unit is a 700 series unit and is covered in the Haynes Fuel Injection book for 86-96 (Haynes # 10220).<P>All the rest is covered in my cave under a number of articles. Start with the 4 cyl QRG, then the DIS notes.<P>Do Not go by the S-10. While similar there are critical diferences.<P>If you really need a book spend the money on <A HREF="http://www.helminc.com" TARGET=_blank>Helm.</A> These are the actual year specific GM shop books. You can also get repalcement Owners manuals and other documents from them.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||jelly2m8||09-05-2001||07:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroPerformance:<BR><B>I have an 85 GT. What is my throttle body supposed to say on it?<P>-Charlie</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>All V6 throttle bodies have HOLLEY rasied on the top||||reg||1
